  <h1 class="hl">Grow Your<br>Own</h1>
  <div class="deck">Some families in Valencia don't wait for the supermarket. They grow it themselves — or share a garden with the neighbours.</div>

  <div class="grid" style="margin-bottom:11px">
    <div class="body-txt" style="flex:1.3">
      <p><span class="dcap">E</span>very week, people go to the supermarket to buy vegetables like green beans and cucumbers that come from big farms. But most people think food from the garden is <strong>fresher</strong> and tastes better.</p>
      <p>Some lucky families have got space to grow food at home — carrots, onions, cabbages. Families without space sometimes work together in a <strong>community garden</strong> instead.</p>
      <p>It's easier than you think. First you <strong>dig</strong>. Then you <strong>plant</strong> the seeds. Remember to <strong>water</strong> the plants! You also <strong>have to weed</strong> the garden sometimes. When the vegetables are <strong>ripe</strong>, they're ready to <strong>pick</strong>.</p>
